Description: mtdev.pc requires linux-input-shim
 The installed mtdev.h includes <linux/input.h>. NextBSD has no
 /usr/include/linux: nextbsd-displayserver-support's linux-input-shim installs
 the header (an #include of the base kernel's <dev/evdev/input.h>) in
 /usr/include/linux-input-shim and adds that directory through its own
 linux-input-shim.pc. Requiring it here makes `pkgconf --cflags mtdev` enough
 to compile against the installed mtdev.h.
Origin: NextBSD (nextbsd/nextbsd-displayserver-support#1, E25)
Forwarded: not-needed
--- a/mtdev.pc.in
+++ b/mtdev.pc.in
@@ -6,5 +6,6 @@
 Name: mtdev
 Description: Multitouch Protocol Translation Library
 Version: @PACKAGE_VERSION@
+Requires: linux-input-shim
 Libs: -L${libdir} -lmtdev
 Cflags: -I${includedir}
